# Documentation Conventions

## Language

- **Authoring language: English.** Concept notes, feature specs, ADRs, reviews, and contributing guides must be written in English (see `AGENTS.md` §5.2a).
- **Product localization** is not documentation: translated UI strings live only in `locales/*.json` (ADR-021).

## Status Tags

Every requirement, feature item, or proposal MUST carry a status tag:

- `STATUS: IDEA` -- Captured but not yet evaluated
- `STATUS: UNDER DISCUSSION` -- Being actively analyzed
- `STATUS: DECIDED` -- Consensus reached, rationale documented
- `STATUS: DEFERRED` -- Postponed to a later phase (include reason and target phase)
- `STATUS: REJECTED` -- Considered and explicitly rejected (include reason)

## User Feature Suggestions

When the user suggests a new feature or idea:
1. ALWAYS write it to `docs/backlog.md` under the matching capability (feature docs are being migrated to OpenSpec, see `docs/openspec-onboarding.md` section 6)
2. Tag it as `STATUS: IDEA` -- do NOT assign a phase unless the user explicitly decides on one
3. Phase assignment happens later when the user reviews and prioritizes ideas
4. If no capability fits, add a new capability heading in `docs/backlog.md`

## Discarded Items

NEVER delete rejected or discarded items. Move them to the "Discarded Alternatives" section of the relevant document with:
- What was proposed
- Why it was rejected
- Who/what triggered the rejection (role review, user decision, technical infeasibility)

## Feature File Template

Feature files in `docs/features/` follow this structure:

```
# Feature: [Name]
## Overview
## Requirements (each with STATUS tag)
## Sub-Features
## Dependencies
## Open Questions
## Discarded Alternatives
```

## ADR Format

Architecture Decision Records in `docs/decisions/` follow this structure:

```
# ADR-NNN: [Title]
- Status: PROPOSED | DECIDED | SUPERSEDED
- Date: YYYY-MM-DD
- Deciders: [who]
## Context
## Options Considered (with Pros/Cons for each)
## Decision
## Consequences
```
